{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short; git branch --show-current; git rev-parse --short HEAD; sed -n '1,160p' docs/design/datom.world.md; cat test/yin/vm/semantic_register/effects_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"?? collab/1791530000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase3-r2.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791530000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase3-r2.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791530000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase3.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791530000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase3.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791530000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase3.report.md\n?? collab/1791550000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4a.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791550000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4a.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791550000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4a.report.md\n?? collab/1791560000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4a.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/1791560000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4a.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791560000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4a.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791580000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4a-r2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791580000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4a-r2.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791580000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4a-r2.report.md\n?? collab/1791590000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4b.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791600000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4a-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/1791600000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4a-r2.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791600000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4a-r2.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791690000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4b-stage1.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791690000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4b-stage1.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791690000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4b-stage1.report.md\n?? collab/1791710000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4b-stage1.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md\n?? collab/1791710000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4b-stage1.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791710000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4b-stage1.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791720000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4b-stage1-r2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791720000000-vm-engineer-srvm-phase4b-stage1-r2.prompt.md\nsrvm-phase4b\ne47fcbd6\n---\ndescription: Core philosophy, foundational axioms, invariants, primitives (tuples, streams, host boundaries), architectural commitments, design principles, code style, and development workflow for datom.world\n---\n\n# DATOM.WORLD ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATIONS & DEVELOPMENT RULES\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nEverything is data.\nInterpretation > abstraction.\nExplicit causality > implicit assumptions.\nRestrictions are a feature.\n\n### Foundational Axioms\n\n1. **Everything is a Stream**: All IO and data flow through append-only streams.\n2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics**: Data is syntax; semantics only emerge through interpretation (one truth, many perspectives).\n   At system scale, a \"system\" is an emergent property of interpreters of\n   pure data, not an object, service, or stored artifact. Find the\n   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\n3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\n4. **Everything is a Continuation**: Computation is modeled as serializable, portable continuations that can pause, travel across streams, and resume anywhere.\n\n## Non-Negotiable Invariants\n\n- Do not introduce hidden global state.\n- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\n- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\n- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\n- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\n- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\n- Do not lose information (unitarity): streams are append-only and no datom is destroyed, only reinterpreted. The Universal AST is never lost: it is always retrievable wherever code is lowered, by address or by a query over its datoms. Every derived form (semantic vector, native images, indexes) is an interpretation of it and may drop facts only because the AST remains.\n\n## Tuples and Datoms\n\nTuples are elements in an open moduli space, graded by dimension $n$. A tuple can be any dimension/size.\nA datom is the canonical persistent tuple `[e a v t m]` (entity, attribute, value, transaction, metadata). Persistent facts are immutable datoms.\nSource scope belongs to the interpreter, never to an appended tuple slot. Queries keep physical sources as separate db-values and express union or joins explicitly.\n\nSee [`docs/design/datom.md`](./datom.md) for full specification.\n\n## Streams\n\nAll IO is modeled as a stream. Functions consume streams and produce streams.\nNo direct function-to-function coupling without a stream boundary.\nSide effects must appear as stream emissions.\nStreams are values that can be sent through streams.\nStreams carry whatever values the consumer needs: no datom requirement, no privileged payload shape.\n\nA stream has no privileged reader, and its meaning is not in it. Any number\nof interpreters may observe the same medium, and each constructs its own\nsemantics from the same batches: a `yin.vm` evaluator observing a program\nstream constructs CESK state and executes it; `dao.space.index` observing\nthe very same stream materializes covered indexes, so `dao.space.query/q`\nanswers Datalog over the program as it grows. Neither knows the other\nexists. The medium is their only coupling, and each observer's ignorance of\nthe other is load-bearing: the evaluator never consults an index to run,\nand the index never evaluates a form to index it. This is how axiom 2\nbecomes architecture: one stream, many interpretations, none of them\nthe stream's own.\n\nFunctions can take anything and return anything.\nAgents are functions, closures, or continuations in `yin.vm` that communicate with the outside world through `dao.stream`. Agent behavior is specified entirely through stream effects.\n\nSee [`docs/design/dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md) for full stream specification.\nSee [`docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md`](./yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md) for VM architecture.\n\n### Host Boundaries\n\nA host boundary is a stream boundary, never a function call. The one\nsanctioned function-shaped contact is a `dao.stream` handle operation, whose\nexhaustive outcome map is stream protocol, not an application callback.\n\n**Effects out.** Portable code appends an effect value describing what must\nhappen. A host interpreter consumes that stream, performs the operation, and\nappends the outcome. Portable code reads the outcome. Correlation is by\nidentity in the data; neither side holds a reference to the other. A host with\nno implementation for an effect emits a qualified unsupported result. That is a\ncorrect outcome, not a gap to be filled.\n\n**Events in.** When the host initiates (a socket receives, a connection drops,\na timer fires) the adapter appends one plain-data event and returns. It invokes\nnothing. An interpreter reads that stream and decides what the event means.\nConstructively: **a callback is replaced by a function that transforms an event\nto data on a stream.** The host's demand for a callback stops at that function.\n\n**Adapters.** An adapter is a map of those transform functions. That is all an\nadapter is. It is a value, not a namespace, and it is general: sockets, files,\ntimers and windows all deliver events by calling something, and an adapter is\nwhat they call. Each entry takes the host's arguments and returns one value;\nthe append is the adapter's, not the entry's, so an entry cannot return a value\nto the host and cannot invoke application code. The adapter is handed only the\ndeposit operation and its own host resource. If its deposit channel fails, it\nmay close that resource to make the boundary observably gone; this is teardown,\nnot an upward callback.\n\nHost types are classified into plain data in the transform: it is the last\nplace holding a host error object, and no host type crosses onto the stream. A\ntransport may use a qualified envelope to preserve correlation, lifecycle, and\nadditive evolution; that envelope remains plain data and creates no separate\nevent mechanism. A composition may likewise define its own qualified vocabulary\nfor facts it owns.\n\nWhich stream an adapter writes to is the caller's composition, never the\nadapter's knowledge. An adapter cannot tell whether it deposits into one\ntransport's private stream or into a medium many interpreters read. This keeps\nthe layering one-way: a boundary depends on nothing above it, because whoever\nconstructs the adapter supplies the stream.\n\nA transform deposits every event admitted by the boundary protocol and judges\nnone of them semantically. Wire framing, decoding, and protocol validation\nhappen below the transform: malformed wire input is transport machinery, not an\nevent. Once the transport has produced a valid host event, data is syntax\n(axiom 2): an event that is noise to one interpreter is signal to another that\ndoes not exist yet, and filtering at the depositing layer destroys perspectives\nnot yet taken. Retention is the medium's operational policy; meaning is\ninterpretation. Neither is the depositor's decision.\n\nTwo things are not adapters. One that exposes a function for portable code to\ncall isolates the host library but keeps the coupling, and the effect never\nappears as an emission. One that takes a function to invoke has relocated the\ncallback, not removed it, even when every value it passes is plain data; if\nthat callback has a meaningful return value, it is a synchronous call in both\ndirections wearing the shape of an event.\n\n## Architectural Commitments\n\n- **`dao.jing` is syntax, agents are semantics**: the content-addressed encoding stays passive and payload-agnostic.\n- **Macros are stream topology**: an evaluator knows nothing about macro expansion; expansion happens on the syntax side of a medium boundary, upstream of any evaluator.\n- **Peer observers, one stream**: a generic evaluator and `dao.space` independently observe the same stream topic, as described under Streams. This is not a claim about any two consumers regardless of what they consume.\n- **Observers are independent and optional**: nothing requires a medium to have any particular set of consumers. Which observers exist for a stream is a per-composition choice, not a design-time commitment.\n\n## Design Principles\n\nCode quality is measured by malleability: how cheaply can changes adapt without breaking promises?\nStigmergic coordination emerges from sharing data across streams.\n\n**Systems emerge from interpreters of pure data.** Streams are the\ncomposition medium; each interpreter gives the same data a perspective\nwithout collapsing interpretation into execution or owning the truth.\n\n- `dao.space` emerges from `dao.space.index` and `dao.space.query` over\n  ordinary streams.\n- ShiBi capability, metering, and budget emerge from different\n  interpreters over the same tuples; no token object is stored.\n- The four VMs interpret one Universal AST; many syntaxes feed that AST.\n- The semantic AST in `dao.space` is queryable facts projected by the\n  auto-index observer.\n- Client and server are roles in one stigmergic behavior implemented by\n  interpreters, not distinct kinds of nodes.\n\n**Derive, don't persist.** Before adding a tag, slot, or field to any\ncanonical content-hashed structure (an AST grammar, a datom schema, a row\nshape), check whether a correctly scoped Datalog query over\n`dao.space.query/q` can already compute the fact. If it can, it belongs as a\nquery or projection: new persisted structure migrates every downstream\nconsumer and duplicates authority over a fact a query derives fresh. The\nretired `:global` tag in\n[`docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md) is the\ncase study, including the scoping bug that a naive query introduced.\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.effects-test\n  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :refer [lit v lam app tail if-node def!]]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.parity-test :as parity]))\n\n\n(defn run-ast\n  ([ast] (vm/run (parity/register-machine ast {:env {'vector vector}})))\n  ([machine ast] (vm/run (sr/load-ast machine (vm/ast->datoms ast) vm/ast-contract))))\n\n\n(defn error\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                 {:message (ex-message e) :data (ex-data e)})))\n\n\n(defn until-inst\n  [machine op]\n  (loop [machine machine fuel 1000]\n    (when (zero? fuel) (throw (ex-info \"Test did not reach instruction\" {:op op})))\n    (let [{:keys [segment pc]} (:control machine)\n          inst (nth (get-in machine [:code segment :vector]) pc)]\n      (if (= op (first inst)) machine (recur (vm/step machine) (dec fuel))))))\n\n\n(defn next-node\n  [cursor]\n  {:type :stream/next :source cursor})\n\n\n(defn put-node\n  [s x]\n  {:type :stream/put :target s :val x})\n\n\n(defn cursor-node\n  [s]\n  {:type :stream/cursor :source s})\n\n\n(defn reader\n  []\n  (parity/register-machine (next-node (cursor-node {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}))))\n\n\n(defn reader-with-live-window\n  []\n  (parity/register-machine\n    (app (v 'vector) (lit nil) (next-node (cursor-node {:type :stream/make :buffer 4})) (lit 2))\n    {:env {'vector vector}}))\n\n\n(deftest non-parking-stream-ops\n  (let [made (run-ast {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}) s (vm/value made)\n        cursor (run-ast made (cursor-node (lit s))) c (vm/value cursor)\n        closed (run-ast cursor {:type :stream/close :source (lit s)})]\n    (is (= :stream-ref (:type s))) (is (:seal s))\n    (is (= :cursor-ref (:type c))) (is (:seal c))\n    (is (nil? (vm/value closed)))\n    (is (vm/halted? closed))))\n\n\n(deftest blocked-read-entry-shape\n  (let [before (until-inst (reader) :stream-next)\n        {:keys [segment pc]} (:control before)\n        rd (second (nth (get-in before [:code segment :vector]) pc))\n        blocked (vm/step before) entry (first (:wait-set blocked))]\n    (is (vm/blocked? blocked))\n    (is (= {:segment segment :pc (inc pc) :env (:env before)\n            :window {} :k [] :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd rd} :reason :next\n            :cursor-ref (:cursor-ref entry) :stream-id (:stream-id entry)} entry))\n    (is (= entry (edn/read-string (pr-str entry))))\n    (is (empty? (:parked blocked)))\n    (is (nil? (:control blocked))) (is (nil? (:k blocked)))))\n\n\n(deftest saved-window-membership\n  (let [before (until-inst (reader-with-live-window) :stream-next)\n        {:keys [segment pc]} (:control before)\n        inst (nth (get-in before [:code segment :vector]) pc) rd (second inst)\n        entry (first (:wait-set (vm/step before)))\n        expected (select-keys (:window before) (analysis/saved (get-in before [:code segment :analysis]) (inc pc) rd))]\n    (is (= expected (:window entry)))\n    (is (= {1 vector 2 nil} (:window entry)))\n    (is (contains? (:window entry) 2))\n    (is (not (contains? (:window entry) rd)))))\n\n\n(deftest wake-delivers-to-rd\n  (let [blocked (vm/run (reader-with-live-window)) entry (first (:wait-set blocked))\n        handle (get (:resources blocked) (:stream-id entry))]\n    (stream/append! handle 7)\n    (let [ready (engine/check-wait-set blocked)\n          restored (engine/resume-from-run-queue ready sr/register-restore)\n          expected (assoc (:window entry) (get-in entry [:deliver :rd]) 7)\n          done (vm/run restored)]\n      (is (= expected (:window restored)))\n      (is (= {:segment (:segment entry) :pc (:pc entry)} (:control restored)))\n      (is (empty? (:ready-queue restored)))\n      (is (= [nil 7 2] (vm/value done)))\n      (is (vm/halted? done)) (is (empty? (:wait-set done))))))\n\n\n;; A bounded transport which can actually answer full (ringbuffer overwrites).\n(defn one-slot-stream\n  [_capacity]\n  (let [slot (atom ::empty) closed? (atom false)]\n    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n     :dao.stream/handle\n     (reify\n       stream/IDaoStreamReader\n       (cursor [_ _anchor] {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n\n       (next\n         [_ _cursor]\n         (if (not= ::empty @slot)\n           (let [value @slot] (reset! slot ::empty)\n                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/value value :dao.stream/cursor 0})\n           {:dao.stream/outcome (if @closed? :dao.stream/end :dao.stream/blocked)}))\n\n\n       stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n       (append!\n         [_ value]\n         (cond @closed? {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/closed}\n               (not= ::empty @slot) {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}\n               :else (do (reset! slot value) {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})))\n\n\n       stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n\n       (close! [_] (reset! closed? true) {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))}))\n\n\n(deftest blocked-put\n  (let [made (vm/run (parity/register-machine {:type :stream/make :buffer 1} {:make-stream one-slot-stream}))\n        s (vm/value made) handle (get (:resources made) (:id s))\n        _ (stream/append! handle :first)\n        blocked (run-ast made (put-node (lit s) (lit :second)))\n        entry (first (:wait-set blocked))]\n    (is (vm/blocked? blocked)) (is (= :put (:reason entry)))\n    (is (= :second (:datom entry))) (is (= {} (:window entry)))\n    (stream/next handle 0)\n    (let [restored (engine/resume-from-run-queue (engine/check-wait-set blocked) sr/register-restore)]\n      (is (= {(get-in entry [:deliver :rd]) :second} (:window restored)))\n      (is (= :second (vm/value (vm/run restored)))))))\n\n\n(deftest terminal-wake-raises\n  (let [made (vm/run (parity/register-machine {:type :stream/make :buffer 1} {:make-stream one-slot-stream}))\n        s (vm/value made) handle (get (:resources made) (:id s))]\n    (stream/append! handle :first)\n    (let [blocked (run-ast made (put-node (lit s) (lit :second)))]\n      (stream/close! handle)\n      (is (re-find #\"Stream append failed\" (:message (error #(vm/run blocked)))))\n      (is (re-find #\"Stream append failed\" (:message (error #(run-ast made (put-node (lit s) (lit :third))))))))))\n\n\n(defn tail-reader\n  [main-tail?]\n  (let [made (run-ast {:type :stream/make :buffer 4})\n        cursor (run-ast made (cursor-node (lit (vm/value made)))) c (vm/value cursor)\n        call (app (lam '[c] (tail (app (v 'stream/next!) (v 'c)))) (lit c))\n        ast (if main-tail? (tail call) (app (v 'vector) (lit nil) call (lit 2)))]\n    (sr/load-ast (assoc cursor :modules (module/register-stream-module (:modules cursor))) (vm/ast->datoms ast) vm/ast-contract)))\n\n\n(deftest tail-effect-returns-through-k\n  (doseq [main-tail? [false true]]\n    (let [blocked (vm/run (tail-reader main-tail?)) entry (first (:wait-set blocked))\n          handle (get (:resources blocked) (:stream-id entry)) frame (peek (:k entry))]\n      (is (vm/blocked? blocked))\n      (is (= #{:segment :site :k :deliver :reason :cursor-ref :stream-id} (set (keys entry))))\n      (is (= {:deliver :return} (:deliver entry)))\n      (is (= (if main-tail? 0 1) (count (:k entry))))\n      (stream/append! handle 9)\n      (let [restored (engine/resume-from-run-queue (engine/check-wait-set blocked) sr/register-restore)]\n        (if main-tail?\n          (do (is (vm/halted? restored)) (is (= 9 (vm/value restored)))\n              (is (not (contains? (:env restored) engine/store-of-key))))\n          (do (is (= (assoc (:window frame) (:rd frame) 9) (:window restored)))\n              (is (= [nil 9 2] (vm/value (vm/run restored))))))))))\n\n\n(deftest tail-primitive-pops-frame\n  (let [ast (app (v 'f) (app (lam '[z] (tail (app (v 'g) (v 'z)))) (v 'x)) (v 'y))\n        before (until-inst (parity/register-machine ast {:env {'f vector 'g inc 'x 7 'y 2}}) :call)\n        entered (vm/step before)\n        call (until-inst entered :call) frame (peek (:k call)) after (vm/step call)]\n    (is (seq (:window frame)))\n    (is (= (assoc (:window frame) (:rd frame) 8) (:window after)))\n    (is (= [8 2] (vm/value (vm/run after))))))\n\n\n(deftest park-resume\n  (let [ast (app (v 'vector) (lit nil) {:type :vm/park} (lit 2))\n        parked (run-ast ast) record (vm/value parked) seg (:program parked)\n        facts (get-in parked [:code seg :analysis]) rd (get-in record [:deliver :rd])]\n    (is (= :parked-0 (:id record)))\n    (is (= :parked-continuation (:type record)))\n    (is (= (select-keys (:window parked) (analysis/saved facts (:pc record) rd)) (:window record)))\n    (is (= {:deliver :rd :rd rd} (:deliver record)))\n    (is (empty? (:wait-set parked)))\n    (let [done (run-ast parked {:type :vm/resume :parked-id (:id record) :val (lit 7)})]\n      (is (= [nil 7 2] (vm/value done))) (is (empty? (:parked done))))\n    (is (re-find #\"not found\" (:message (error #(run-ast parked {:type :vm/resume :parked-id :missing :val (lit 1)}))))))\n  (let [parked (vm/run (parity/register-machine {:type :vm/park})) record (vm/value parked)]\n    (is (= {:type :parked-continuation :id :parked-0 :segment (:program parked)\n            :pc 1 :env {} :window {} :k [] :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd 0}} record))\n    (is (= record (edn/read-string (pr-str record))))))\n\n\n(deftest resume-return-mode\n  (doseq [frame? [false true]]\n    (let [base (parity/register-machine (app (v 'vector) (lit :saved) (lit 7)) {:env {'vector vector}})\n          seg (:program base)\n          frame {:type :return :segment seg :pc 3 :env {} :window {1 vector 2 :saved} :rd 3}\n          base (assoc-in base [:parked :p] {:segment seg :site 0 :k (if frame? [frame] []) :deliver {:deliver :return}})\n          done (run-ast base {:type :vm/resume :parked-id :p :val (lit 9)})]\n      (is (= (if frame? [:saved 9] 9) (vm/value done)))\n      (is (vm/halted? done)) (is (empty? (:parked done))))))\n\n\n(deftest reified-shape\n  (let [machine (parity/register-machine {:type :vm/current-continuation})\n        seg (:program machine) after (vm/step machine)\n        k (get (:window after) 0) payload (values/payload k)]\n    (is (values/continuation? k))\n    (is (= {:type :reified-continuation :segment seg :pc 1 :env {} :window {} :k [] :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd 0}} payload))\n    (is (= payload (edn/read-string (pr-str payload))))))\n\n\n(deftest foreign-continuation-refused\n  (let [k (values/continuation :other {})\n        data (:data (error #(vm/run (parity/register-machine (app (v 'k) (lit 1)) {:env {'k k}}))))]\n    (is (= {:reason :foreign-value :kind :continuation} (select-keys data [:reason :kind])))))\n\n\n(deftest store-and-gensym-test\n  (let [ast (app (v 'vector) {:type :vm/gensym} {:type :stream/make :buffer 4} {:type :vm/gensym :prefix \"g\"})\n        done (run-ast ast) [a s b] (vm/value done)]\n    (is (= :id-0 a)) (is (= :stream-1 (:id s))) (is (= :g-2 b))\n    (is (= 3 (:id-counter done)))))\n\n\n(deftest window-is-a-gc-root\n  (let [modules (module/register-cell-module (module/default-registry))\n        result (vm/run (parity/register-machine (app (v 'vector) (app (v 'cell/new) (lit :keep)) (app (v 'cell/new) (lit :junk))) {:modules modules :env {'vector vector}}))\n        [keep-ref] (vm/value result)\n        only-window (assoc result :env {} :control nil :k nil :value nil :window {0 keep-ref})\n        collected (engine/collect only-window)]\n    (is (= #{:keep} (set (map :value (vals (:heap collected))))))\n    (is (= #{} (set (map :value (vals (:heap (engine/collect (assoc only-window :window {}))))))))))\n\n\n;; The five continuation programs are respelled here; backend registration is stage 2.\n(def capture {:type :vm/current-continuation})\n\n\n(defn then\n  [a b]\n  (parity/then a b))\n\n\n(defn with-k\n  [body]\n  (app (lam '[r] body) capture))\n\n\n(defn every-vm=\n  [expected ast]\n  (let [result (try {:machine (run-ast ast)}\n                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                      {:thrown (ex-message e)}))]\n    (if-let [done (:machine result)]\n      (do (is (= expected (vm/value done))) (is (vm/halted? done)))\n      (is (= expected [:thrown (:thrown result)])))))\n\n\n(deftest escape-discards-pending-frames-test\n  (testing \"invoked under (+ 1000 ...), the continuation delivers 7 to the\n            capture point: the +1000 frame is discarded, the captured +1\n            frame is not\"\n    (every-vm= 9\n               (app (v '+)\n                    (lit 1)\n                    (with-k (if-node (app (v '=) (v 'r) (lit 7))\n                                     (app (v '+) (v 'r) (lit 1))\n                                     (app (v '+)\n                                          (lit 1000)\n                                          (app (v 'r) (lit 7)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest tail-position-invocation-test\n  (testing \"the continuation invoked as a tail call\"\n    (every-vm= 8\n               (app (v '+)\n                    (lit 1)\n                    (with-k (if-node (app (v '=) (v 'r) (lit 7))\n                                     (v 'r)\n                                     (tail (app (v 'r) (lit 7)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest re-entry-after-return-test\n  (testing \"a continuation captured inside a returned call, kept in the\n            store, re-enters its capture point once per invocation; the\n            counter bounds the loop\"\n    ;; count <- 0\n    ;; x <- ((fn [] (current-continuation)))   ; returns before any invoke\n    ;; when count = 0: saved <- x\n    ;; if count < 3: count <- count + 1, (saved (* 10 count)) else [x count]\n    (every-vm=\n      [30 3]\n      (then\n        (def! 'count (lit 0))\n        (app (lam ['x]\n                  (then (if-node (app (v '=) (v 'count) (lit 0))\n                                 (def! 'saved (v 'x))\n                                 (lit nil))\n                        (if-node (app (v '<) (v 'count) (lit 3))\n                                 (then (def! 'count\n                                         (app (v '+) (v 'count) (lit 1)))\n                                       (app (v 'saved)\n                                            (app (v '*)\n                                                 (lit 10)\n                                                 (v 'count))))\n                                 (app (v 'conj)\n                                      (app (v 'conj) (lit []) (v 'x))\n                                      (v 'count)))))\n             (app (lam [] capture)))))))\n\n\n(deftest store-not-rolled-back-test\n  (testing \"a store write made before the invocation is visible after it\"\n    (every-vm= [1 :written]\n               (with-k (if-node (app (v '=) (v 'r) (lit 1))\n                                (app (v 'conj)\n                                     (app (v 'conj) (lit []) (v 'r))\n                                     (v 'mark))\n                                (then (def! 'mark (lit :written))\n                                      (app (v 'r) (lit 1))))))))\n\n\n(deftest arity-error-identical-across-vms-test\n  (doseq [argc [0 2]]\n    (testing (str argc \" arguments\")\n      (every-vm= [:thrown \"Continuation expects exactly one argument\"]\n                 (with-k (if-node (app (v '=) (v 'r) (lit 1))\n                                  (v 'r)\n                                  (apply app (v 'r)\n                                         (repeat argc (lit 1)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest stream-outcomes-and-edn-wake\n  (let [blocked (vm/run (reader)) entry (first (:wait-set blocked))\n        revived (assoc blocked :wait-set (edn/read-string (pr-str (:wait-set blocked))))\n        handle (get (:resources blocked) (:stream-id entry))\n        cursor-id (get-in entry [:cursor-ref :id])\n        before (get-in blocked [:resources cursor-id :cursor])]\n    (is (vm/blocked? (vm/run blocked)))\n    (stream/append! handle :from-edn)\n    (let [done (vm/run revived)]\n      (is (= :from-edn (vm/value done)))\n      (is (not= before (get-in done [:resources cursor-id :cursor])))))\n  (let [blocked (vm/run (reader)) entry (first (:wait-set blocked))]\n    (stream/close! (get (:resources blocked) (:stream-id entry)))\n    (is (nil? (vm/value (vm/run blocked)))))\n  (let [blocked (vm/run (reader)) entry (first (:wait-set blocked))\n        handle (get (:resources blocked) (:stream-id entry))]\n    (dotimes [n 8] (stream/append! handle n))\n    (is (= :dao.stream/gap (vm/value (vm/run blocked)))))\n  (let [made (run-ast {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}) s (vm/value made)\n        put (run-ast made (put-node (lit s) (lit 7)))\n        handle (get (:resources put) (:id s))\n        cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest))]\n    (is (= 7 (vm/value put)))\n    (is (= 7 (:dao.stream/value (stream/next handle cursor)))))\n  (is (some? (error #(run-ast (put-node (lit {:type :stream-ref :id :missing}) (lit 1)))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
